            <ArticleTitle>Are monitored telemetry beds necessary for patients with nontraumatic chest pain and normal or nonspecific electrocardiograms?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1110-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We evaluated the frequency of cardiovascular complications in chest pain patients with normal or non-specific electrocardiograms admitted to noncardiac care unit monitored beds and found that none of 261 patients had life-threatening dysrrhythmias requiring treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
